      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Admitting that immediate aid is not a cure-all for every underlying problem would be an unnecessary admission of defeat that we can ill afford to make. While true that aid must be paired with long-term development, deciding that we will not help those in immediate crisis is like refusing to treat the poisoning victim just because a vaccine is ten years away. Such an argument is not a critique of inefficiency, but rather a convenient excuse for us to absolve ourselves of the most urgent moral duty we can take. To claim we can do nothing about the spectacle of suffering while it is still within our power to act is to choose selfishness over the very essence of humanity.",
